  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: conditions_appsec_rule_names
  required: false
  type: string
  underlyingargname: conditions_appsec_rule_names
- description: |
    A comma-separated list of AppSec rule categories to filter findings. Applies to SECRETS and IAC_MISCONFIGURATION finding types.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: conditions_appsec_rule_category
  required: false
  type: string
  underlyingargname: conditions_appsec_rule_category
- description: |
    CVSS base score threshold for vulnerability findings (0.0-10.0). Only vulnerabilities meeting or exceeding this score will trigger the policy.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: conditions_cvss
  required: false
  type: number
  underlyingargname: conditions_cvss
- description: |
    Exploit Prediction Scoring System (EPSS) score threshold (0–100). Filters vulnerabilities based on their predicted likelihood of exploitation. This filter is applied only when an explicit request to evaluate by EPSS or exploit probability is provided.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: conditions_epss
  required: false
  type: number
  underlyingargname: conditions_epss
- description: |
    Filters by the Common Vulnerability Scoring System impact level, often derived from a numerical score (e.g., Critical, High, Medium, or Low). Options: Critical, High, Medium, Low.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: conditions_cvss_severity
  required: false
  type: string
  underlyingargname: conditions_cvss_severity
- description: |
    Filter findings based on whether a remediation fix or patch is available. Options: true, false.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: conditions_has_a_fix
  required: false
  type: boolean
  underlyingargname: conditions_has_a_fix
- description: |
    Targets findings listed in the Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV) catalog, indicating confirmed real-world exploitation. Suitable when filtering for exploitable or known-exploited vulnerabilities.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: conditions_is_kev
  required: false
  type: boolean
  underlyingargname: conditions_is_kev
- description: |
